Chapter 6: Idempotency and Logical Purchase Uniqueness

6.1 Definitions

Request deduplication. A payment provider may deduplicate identical requests under an idempotency key with a bounded TTL (typically 24 hours). This does not guarantee logical uniqueness.

Logical purchase uniqueness. For principal u, intent i, and authorized checkout C, define:

P_{\mathrm{id}} = H(u,\ i,\ h_c)

P_{\mathrm{id}} is a logical purchase identifier. Two submissions with the same P_{\mathrm{id}} represent the same intended purchase.

On the inclusion of h_c. P_{\mathrm{id}} includes the checkout hash, so a re-priced checkout produces a different logical purchase. This is deliberate. A re-priced checkout is a different offer with different terms; treating it as the same logical purchase would allow a merchant to substitute terms under a stable identity. The consequence is that P_{\mathrm{id}} does not, by itself, prevent a double charge across a price change. That case is handled by reconciliation using the tuple (i, u), which is stable across re-pricing.

Correction from earlier drafts. The tuple (P_{\mathrm{id}}, \mathrm{intent\_id}) is redundant because P_{\mathrm{id}} already includes i. The reconciliation key must be (i, u), not (P_{\mathrm{id}}, \mathrm{intent\_id}).

6.2 Participant Capability Contract

Each merchant adapter declares a capability vector:

\kappa_m = (\kappa_{\mathrm{idem}},\ \kappa_{\mathrm{status}},\ \kappa_{\mathrm{stable\_id}},\ \kappa_{\mathrm{pay\_status}},\ \kappa_{\mathrm{recon}})

where each component is in \{0, 1\}.

If \kappa_{\mathrm{idem}} = 0 or \kappa_{\mathrm{recon}} = 0, the orchestrator MUST mark the outcome as UNCERTAIN after any ambiguous response and MUST NOT automatically retry. The capability vector is self-declared; a malicious adapter may misrepresent its capabilities. This is an explicit assumption, not a verified property. Merchant adapter attestation is a candidate for M4.

6.3 Reconciliation Obligation

For any attempt with an ambiguous outcome:

\mathrm{Ambiguous}(o) \Rightarrow \mathrm{Obligation}(\mathrm{Reconcile}(o))

Reconciliation queries the merchant using (i, u, \mathrm{attempt\_id}, P_{\mathrm{id}}^{\mathrm{old}}). Outcomes: CONFIRMED, FAILED, UNKNOWN. UNKNOWN after a bounded number of attempts escalates to human review.

6.4 Limitation

No orchestration layer can guarantee exactly-once external execution across arbitrary merchants without cooperation or enforceable guarantees from those participants. UACN treats this as a documented limitation, not a solved problem. The useful guarantee is one committed business effect per operation identity, which is weaker than exactly-once and stronger than at-most-once.

---

Chapter 7: Revocation and In-Flight Semantics

7.1 State Partition

\mathcal{S}_{\mathrm{rev}} = \{\mathrm{REVOKED},\ \mathrm{SUBMISSION\_IN\_FLIGHT},\ \mathrm{SUBMITTED},\ \mathrm{CANCEL\_REQUESTED},\ \mathrm{CANCEL\_CONFIRMED},\ \mathrm{COMP\_FAILED}\}

These are distinct states, not interchangeable descriptions of a successful revocation. The formal model uses REVOKED as a flag on the authorization object and SUBMITTING as the phase; this partition is a policy-level abstraction that maps to the model's state space.

7.2 Policy

· Before t_\ell: revocation prevents submission.
· After t_\ell: revocation prevents further unauthorized actions but does not falsely claim to reverse the external operation.
· Cancellation is initiated through a separate, authenticated merchant workflow where available.
· Payment capture, cancellation, and refund status are independently tracked.

7.3 Formal Statement

Let t_r be the time of revocation and t_\ell the linearization point.

t_r < t_\ell \Rightarrow \mathrm{Submitted}(o) = \mathrm{false}

t_r \geq t_\ell \Rightarrow \mathrm{Submitted}(o) \in \{\mathrm{true},\ \mathrm{unknown}\}

The control plane MUST NOT assert \mathrm{Submitted}(o) = \mathrm{false} after t_\ell without reconciliation evidence.

---

Chapter 8: Formal Model

8.1 Model Structure

The model is a single composed TLA+ module, OrderLifecycle.tla. It covers authorization lifecycle, order submission, payment state, and compensation state in one state space, because the invariants of interest cross all four concerns. Sub-module decomposition is deferred to a later milestone, when multi-merchant orchestration introduces independent state spaces that justify the modular boundary.

The environment is modeled as a nondeterministic component producing delayed responses, lost responses, duplicate messages, and unavailable services.

8.2 State Variables

S_t = (I_t,\ A_t,\ O_t,\ P_t,\ R_t,\ L_t)

where I_t is the purchase intent, A_t is the authorization state, O_t is the order state, P_t is the payment state, R_t is the reconciliation state, and L_t is the append-only audit log.

8.3 TLA+ Module

The following module is designed to execute in TLC with a finite configuration. The full specification is maintained in formal/OrderLifecycle.tla.

```tla
------------------------------ MODULE OrderLifecycle ------------------------------
EXTENDS Integers, Sequences, TLC, FiniteSets

CONSTANTS Principal, Intent, Merchant, MaxTime, Checkout

VARIABLES
    now, phase, auth, attempt, submitted, providerStatus,
    orderState, paymentState, compState, audit, submitAuthValid

vars == <<now, phase, auth, attempt, submitted, providerStatus,
          orderState, paymentState, compState, audit, submitAuthValid>>

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
\* Types

TypeOK ==
    /\ now \in 0..MaxTime
    /\ phase \in {"DRAFT", "INTENT_VALIDATED", "SEARCHING", "OFFERS_RECEIVED",
                  "FILTERED", "RANKED", "AWAITING_APPROVAL", "AUTHORIZED",
                  "SUBMITTING", "AMBIGUOUS", "RECONCILING",
                  "CONFIRMED", "FAILED", "CANCELLED", "CANCEL_REQUESTED"}
    /\ auth.principal = Principal
    /\ auth.intent = Intent
    /\ auth.merchant = Merchant
    /\ auth.scope = "single_use"
    /\ auth.used \in BOOLEAN
    /\ auth.revoked \in BOOLEAN
    /\ auth.amount \in Nat
    /\ auth.currency \in {Checkout.currency}
    /\ auth.checkout_hash \in STRING \cup {<<>>}
    /\ auth.expires_at \in 0..MaxTime
    /\ attempt.id \in Nat
    /\ attempt.amount \in Nat
    /\ attempt.currency \in {Checkout.currency}
    /\ attempt.checkout_hash \in STRING \cup {<<>>}
    /\ submitted \subseteq Nat
    /\ providerStatus \in [submitted -> {"unknown", "confirmed", "failed"}]
    /\ submitAuthValid \in BOOLEAN
    /\ orderState \in {"NONE", "PENDING", "CONFIRMED", "FAILED", "CANCELLED"}
    /\ paymentState \in {"NONE", "AUTHORIZED", "CAPTURED", "REFUNDED"}
    /\ compState \in {"NONE", "CANCEL_REQUESTED", "CANCEL_CONFIRMED",
                      "REFUND_REQUESTED", "REFUND_CONFIRMED", "FAILED"}
    /\ Len(audit) >= 0

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
\* Authorization validity

AuthValid(a) ==
    /\ a.principal = Principal
    /\ a.intent = Intent
    /\ a.merchant = Merchant
    /\ a.checkout_hash = Checkout.hash
    /\ a.amount = Checkout.amount
    /\ a.currency = Checkout.currency
    /\ a.scope = "single_use"
    /\ a.revoked = FALSE
    /\ a.used = FALSE
    /\ now < a.expires_at

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
\* Initial state

Init ==
    /\ now = 0
    /\ phase = "DRAFT"
    /\ auth = [ principal |-> Principal, intent |-> Intent,
                merchant |-> Merchant, checkout_hash |-> <<>>,
                amount |-> 0, currency |-> Checkout.currency,
                expires_at |-> 0, nonce |-> 0,
                scope |-> "single_use",
                revoked |-> FALSE, used |-> FALSE ]
    /\ attempt = [ id |-> 0, checkout_hash |-> <<>>,
                   amount |-> 0, currency |-> Checkout.currency ]
    /\ submitted = {}
    /\ providerStatus = [ a \in {} |-> "unknown" ]
    /\ orderState = "NONE"
    /\ paymentState = "NONE"
    /\ compState = "NONE"
    /\ audit = <<>>
    /\ submitAuthValid = FALSE

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
\* Pre-submission transitions

ValidateIntent ==
    /\ phase = "DRAFT"
    /\ phase' = "INTENT_VALIDATED"
    /\ UNCHANGED <<now, auth, attempt, submitted, providerStatus,
                    orderState, paymentState, compState, submitAuthValid>>
    /\ audit' = Append(audit, [t |-> now, ev |-> "validate_intent"])

Search ==
    /\ phase = "INTENT_VALIDATED"
    /\ phase' = "SEARCHING"
    /\ UNCHANGED <<now, auth, attempt, submitted, providerStatus,
                    orderState, paymentState, compState, submitAuthValid>>
    /\ audit' = Append(audit, [t |-> now, ev |-> "start_search"])

ReceiveOffers ==
    /\ phase = "SEARCHING"
    /\ phase' = "OFFERS_RECEIVED"
    /\ now' = now + 1
    /\ UNCHANGED <<auth, attempt, submitted, providerStatus,
                    orderState, paymentState, compState, submitAuthValid>>
    /\ audit' = Append(audit, [t |-> now, ev |-> "receive_offers"])

Filter ==
    /\ phase = "OFFERS_RECEIVED"
    /\ phase' = "FILTERED"
    /\ UNCHANGED <<now, auth, attempt, submitted, providerStatus,
                    orderState, paymentState, compState, submitAuthValid>>
    /\ audit' = Append(audit, [t |-> now, ev |-> "filter_hard_constraints"])

Rank ==
    /\ phase = "FILTERED"
    /\ phase' = "RANKED"
    /\ UNCHANGED <<now, auth, attempt, submitted, providerStatus,
                    orderState, paymentState, compState, submitAuthValid>>
    /\ audit' = Append(audit, [t |-> now, ev |-> "rank"])

RequestApproval ==
    /\ phase = "RANKED"
    /\ phase' = "AWAITING_APPROVAL"
    /\ UNCHANGED <<now, auth, attempt, submitted, providerStatus,
                    orderState, paymentState, compState, submitAuthValid>>
    /\ audit' = Append(audit, [t |-> now, ev |-> "request_approval"])

Approve ==
    /\ phase = "AWAITING_APPROVAL"
    /\ phase' = "AUTHORIZED"
    /\ auth' = [ auth EXCEPT
                   !.checkout_hash = Checkout.hash,
                   !.amount        = Checkout.amount,
                   !.currency      = Checkout.currency,
                   !.expires_at    = now + 3,
                   !.used          = FALSE ]
    /\ UNCHANGED <<now, attempt, submitted, providerStatus,
                    orderState, paymentState, compState, submitAuthValid>>
    /\ audit' = Append(audit, [t |-> now, ev |-> "approve"])

\* Revocation before submission
Revoke ==
    /\ phase = "AUTHORIZED"
    /\ phase' = "CANCELLED"
    /\ auth' = [ auth EXCEPT !.revoked = TRUE ]
    /\ UNCHANGED <<now, attempt, submitted, providerStatus,
                    orderState, paymentState, compState, submitAuthValid>>
    /\ audit' = Append(audit, [t |-> now, ev |-> "revoke_before_submit"])

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
\* Submission and environment nondeterminism

\* Linearization point: atomically consume authorization and record attempt.
\* submitAuthValid records whether the authorization was valid at t_ell.
Submit ==
    /\ phase = "AUTHORIZED"
    /\ AuthValid(auth)
    /\ attempt.id + 1 \notin submitted
    /\ phase' = "SUBMITTING"
    /\ auth' = [ auth EXCEPT !.used = TRUE ]
    /\ attempt' = [ attempt EXCEPT
                      !.id = attempt.id + 1,
                      !.checkout_hash = Checkout.hash,
                      !.amount = Checkout.amount,
                      !.currency = Checkout.currency ]
    /\ submitted' = submitted \cup {attempt.id + 1}
    /\ submitAuthValid' = AuthValid(auth)
    /\ providerStatus' = providerStatus @@ (attempt.id + 1 :> "unknown")
    /\ orderState' = "PENDING"
    /\ UNCHANGED <<now, paymentState, compState>>
    /\ audit' = Append(audit, [t |-> now, ev |-> "submit"])

\* Environment responses
ProviderConfirm ==
    /\ phase = "SUBMITTING"
    /\ phase' = "CONFIRMED"
    /\ now' = now + 1
    /\ providerStatus' = providerStatus @@ (attempt.id :> "confirmed")
    /\ orderState' = "CONFIRMED"
    /\ UNCHANGED <<auth, attempt, submitted, paymentState, compState, submitAuthValid>>
    /\ audit' = Append(audit, [t |-> now, ev |-> "provider_confirmed"])

ProviderFail ==
    /\ phase = "SUBMITTING"
    /\ phase' = "FAILED"
    /\ now' = now + 1
    /\ providerStatus' = providerStatus @@ (attempt.id :> "failed")
    /\ orderState' = "FAILED"
    /\ UNCHANGED <<auth, attempt, submitted, paymentState, compState, submitAuthValid>>
    /\ audit' = Append(audit, [t |-> now, ev |-> "provider_failed"])

ProviderTimeout ==
    /\ phase = "SUBMITTING"
    /\ phase' = "AMBIGUOUS"
    /\ now' = now + 1
    /\ providerStatus' = providerStatus @@ (attempt.id :> "unknown")
    /\ UNCHANGED <<auth, attempt, submitted, orderState, paymentState, compState, submitAuthValid>>
    /\ audit' = Append(audit, [t |-> now, ev |-> "provider_timeout"])

\* Reconciliation: environment may update provider status asynchronously.
Reconcile ==
    /\ phase = "AMBIGUOUS"
    /\ phase' = "RECONCILING"
    /\ UNCHANGED <<now, auth, attempt, submitted, providerStatus,
                    orderState, paymentState, compState, submitAuthValid>>
    /\ audit' = Append(audit, [t |-> now, ev |-> "reconcile"])

\* Environment resolves the attempt during reconciliation.
ReconcileResolve ==
    /\ phase = "RECONCILING"
    /\ providerStatus[attempt.id] = "unknown"
    /\ \/ providerStatus' = providerStatus @@ (attempt.id :> "confirmed")
       \/ providerStatus' = providerStatus @@ (attempt.id :> "failed")
    /\ now' = now + 1
    /\ UNCHANGED <<auth, attempt, submitted, orderState, paymentState, compState, submitAuthValid>>
    /\ audit' = Append(audit, [t |-> now, ev |-> "reconcile_resolve"])

ReconcileConfirmed ==
    /\ phase = "RECONCILING"
    /\ providerStatus[attempt.id] = "confirmed"
    /\ phase' = "CONFIRMED"
    /\ orderState' = "CONFIRMED"
    /\ UNCHANGED <<now, auth, attempt, submitted, providerStatus,
                    paymentState, compState, submitAuthValid>>
    /\ audit' = Append(audit, [t |-> now, ev |-> "reconcile_confirmed"])

ReconcileFailed ==
    /\ phase = "RECONCILING"
    /\ providerStatus[attempt.id] = "failed"
    /\ phase' = "FAILED"
    /\ orderState' = "FAILED"
    /\ UNCHANGED <<now, auth, attempt, submitted, providerStatus,
                    paymentState, compState, submitAuthValid>>
    /\ audit' = Append(audit, [t |-> now, ev |-> "reconcile_failed"])

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
\* Compensation as a new operation

RequestCancel ==
    /\ phase = "CONFIRMED"
    /\ phase' = "CANCEL_REQUESTED"
    /\ compState' = "CANCEL_REQUESTED"
