Chapter 9: Candidate Invariants

These are proposed properties to formalize and test, not proven theorems. INV-1 through INV-7 are the model-checked invariants of Chapter 8; the remaining are implementation-level candidates.

Invariant 1 — Authorization soundness. At the linearization point, the authorization was valid. Model-checked as INV-1.

Invariant 2 — Hard-constraint preservation. Submitted orders satisfy the encoded hard constraints of the intent. This is an implementation-level property, tested in tests/property/, not a model-checked invariant.

Invariant 3 — Secret isolation. Payment credentials and other financial secrets are not exposed to the reasoning plane. Expressed as an information-flow property.

Invariant 4 — Uncertainty preservation. Model-checked as INV-4.

Invariant 5 — Audit integrity. Every authorization, submission attempt, external response, revocation, and compensation transition is associated with a traceable event, and the log is append-only. The model-level invariant checks timestamp monotonicity; the implementation-level property includes append-only enforcement and per-entry signatures.

Invariant 6 — Compensation soundness. Model-checked as INV-6.

Invariant 7 — Cancellation soundness. Model-checked as INV-7.

