For each threat T with adversary class A and mitigation M, the mitigation obligation is:

\mathrm{Detectable}(T, M) \wedge \mathrm{Bounded}(T, M)

where Detectable means the mitigation provides evidence of an attempted exploitation, and Bounded means the mitigation restricts the damage to a defined set of states.

