6. Authorization Object A — Structure & Binding

```
   ┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
   │                       AUTHORIZATION OBJECT  A                      │
   │                                                                    │
   │   A = ( u, i, m, h_c, a, c, e, n, s, σ_u, σ_m )                    │
   │                                                                    │
   │   u   authenticated consumer        σ_u  consumer signature         │
   │   i   purchase intent id            σ_m  merchant signature         │
   │   m   merchant identity                                            │
   │   h_c checkout hash                                                │
   │   a   authorized amount                                            │
   │   c   currency                                                     │
   │   e   expiration                                                   │
   │   n   unique nonce                                                 │
   │   s   permitted scope                                              │
   └────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

   Canonical checkout C:
     C = Canon( merchant_id, line_items, taxes, shipping, discounts,
                total, currency, delivery_terms )

     Canonicalization rules:
       • field ordering: lexicographic by UTF-8 byte
       • numbers: decimal strings, fixed scale, no float
       • currency: ISO 4217 alphabetic
       • line items: sorted by stable SKU; integer quantities
       • absent fields: omitted, not null
       • whitespace: stripped (except within string values)
       • Unicode: NFC

     h_c = SHA-256( C )

   SD-JWT encoding (AP2-compatible), with UACN extension claims:
     uacn_p_id      = P_id = H(u, i, h_c)
     uacn_context   = ctx  = H(m, h_c, P_id, n)
     uacn_capability= κ_m  = (κ_idem, κ_status, κ_stable_id,
                              κ_pay_status, κ_recon)

   ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
   │   σ_m over C  ───►  h_c  ───►  bound into A  ───►  σ_u over A │
   │                                                              │
   │   substitution of a different checkout invalidates σ_u       │
   └──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
