13. Experimental Design — Four Conditions

```
   ┌──────────┬──────────────────┬────────────┬─────────────────────────────────┐
   │ COND.    │ WORKFLOW         │ INTERFACE  │ MEASURES                        │
   ├──────────┼──────────────────┼────────────┼─────────────────────────────────┤
   │   A      │ Manual shopping  │ Human-only │ baseline (benchmark, not ctrl)  │
   │   B      │ Conventional     │ Structured │ agent baseline w/o UACN ctrl    │
   │          │ agent shopping   │            │ plane                           │
   │   C      │ Deterministic    │ Structured │ value of UACN ctrl plane        │
   │          │ UACN             │            │ without LLM proposals           │
   │   D      │ LLM-assisted     │ Structured │ incremental contribution of     │
   │          │ UACN             │            │ LLM inside UACN ctrl plane      │
   └──────────┴──────────────────┴────────────┴─────────────────────────────────┘

   Common intent interface across B, C, D — otherwise the interface
   itself is part of the treatment.

   Estimands:
     Δ_LLM  = E[Y | UACN_LLM]          − E[Y | UACN_deterministic]
     Δ_UACN = E[Y | UACN_deterministic]− E[Y | Conventional_agent]

   Δ_UACN is a BUNDLE effect; it does not decompose into individual
   mechanisms. Decomposition requires additional conditions varying
   one mechanism at a time.

   Primary outcome: hard-constraint violation rate.
   Pre-registration required before confirmatory results.
   Controlled catalog with known ground truth before real merchants.
```

